hinking i'll be  nervous the morning of and then i'll be  nervous right ahead of launch and it  never really happened  but i know exactly that emotion you're  talking about  i felt it reflected from my kids and my  mom  and my dad all whom were nervous for us  yes  they were afraid i could see that no  matter what we did to try and settle  them down and calm them and  we really couldn't get there and then to  see their relief  they were you know more tearful after we  landed and came out the  capsule that's when they really broke  down yeah  and they were just so relieved and they  could finally  let it all out your mom was the first  one you hugged when you got off  was there clearly it's a bonding moment  for the two of you did you have a moment  with the two of you  up there we did my brother and i were we  picked seats so that we could see each  other from our seats  so we could look over and and and we had  we did you sit in the jeff bezos chair  okay  i'm gonna sit in chair number five we  got a chance to see what those seats  were like  the bezos brothers gave me a ground  level view of their training capsule  i think we were a little surprised by  how intense the  g-forces were on you know the kind of  ascent you know your  skin's all being pulled back into your  face and you're pushed into your seat  mark they tried to do a a comms check or  a status check with mark while we were  at max g's on return  yeah it was just bad timing though by  the time it got to you know they went  through oliver and wally by the time it  got to me  we were at five g's which is what it  said right here and they were like you  know astronaut mark how are you doing i  was  like  [Music]  i had a hard time responding to that one  so what's next because jeff you don't  have to do anything  but you choose to do one of the hardest  things well  you you do the things that you're  passionate about gail  if you're lucky in life you know you can  have a job you can have a career if  you're really lucky you get to have a  calling  i want people to know that besides being  a successful businessman you are still a  volunteer firefighter  and you did a ted talk people have to  look at it it's about kindness  but jeff said since you already have the  kindness gene  you already have the success gene he  said that this  changed him how did it change you  i think that i'm still processing a lot  of that  um but i will tell you in the um  in the best sense i've never felt  smaller  than i did today and it was and  it was um just an incredibly  humbling and beautiful sense of  personal scale right that i am such a  small part of all of this  i know look at the earth up there and it  will make you more humble  yeah i can't imagine what it was like i  thought it was great that we got to go  in that capsule together i call that a  basil sandwich i go  look at us guys we're basil sandwiches  i'm the filling nope i would call it  that but okay  no i thought that was funny they thought  it was funny too vlad all right  but listen you know there's been a lot  of talk about all the money that was  spent and  how he's you know how he spends his  money i love people trying to tell him  how to spend his own money  but yesterday he did something that was  also jaw-dropping it sure was  courage and civility award that's  getting lost in this coverage of the  of the space launch which is monumental  but he gave the courage and civility  award the first  to two people van jones and chef jose  andres  and it's to give to them to distribute  to charities and non-profits of their  choice  singling out people that he thinks are  doing hard work and doing it with  civility  it was jaw-dropping and he gave them a  hundred million  did i not say that part number no yeah  thank you anthony millions  that was a jaw-dropping part and they  can do whatever they want  yes no strings attached you two decide  how the money is best spent you know van  has done a lot of work with crimina